  details[32]{code,credits,slug,desc}:
    LAW4010H,3,foundations-canadian-law,"An introduction to the Canadian legal system: sources of authority, separation of powers, judicial review and common law reasoning, with attention to Aboriginal peoples and international law."
    LAW4001H,3,law-and-business-global-economy,"The business law groundwork for the rest of the program, covering corporate governance, securities regulation, insolvency and financial oversight."
    LAW4026H,3,introduction-law-and-technology,"Starts from first-year foundations in torts, contracts, property, constitutional and criminal law, then asks how technology reshapes each of them and the justice system with them."
    LAW4008H,3,canadian-constitutional-law,"How Canada's Constitution is structured and interpreted: the division of powers between governments, and the rights it protects, from expression and religion to equality and Indigenous rights."
    LAW4009H,3,canadian-criminal-law,"The fundamentals of criminal liability: where offences come from, intent and causation, extensions of liability, the defences, and procedure through sentencing and appeal."
    LAW4032H,3,intellectual-property-law,"Patents, trademarks, copyright and neighbouring rights treated as an asset class, and how they work strategically for a business, especially in technology."
    LAW4002H,3,comparative-corporate-governance,"The relationships between a company, its directors, management, shareholders and stakeholders, how ESG commitments shape decisions, and what governance failures teach about prevention."
    LAW4017H,3,professional-responsibility,"The principles governing lawyers' conduct in Canada, centred on the Model Code of Professional Conduct, and how lawyers are licensed and regulated across jurisdictions."
    LAW4046H,3,privacy-and-data-governance,"Privacy law and how it applies to emerging technology, including AI, data aggregation, surveillance and online advertising, seen from the consumer, business and regulator sides."
    LAW4055H,3,disruptive-innovations-legal-infrastructure,"Where innovation and regulation fall out of step as new products reach market, and how shifts in legal technology, regulation and funding may reshape legal services."
    LAW4072H,3,aboriginal-law,"The legal history of Indigenous-Crown relations from contact through treaties and the Indian Act, then the live questions: Aboriginal rights, modern agreements, the duty to consult and UNDRIP."
    LAW4007H,3,canadian-administrative-law,"How government actually operates: the procedures, limits and jurisdiction of agencies and tribunals, and when public bodies answer to administrative law rather than to contract or tort."
    LAW4036H,3,applied-contract-law,"Contract principles worked through business situations rather than doctrine alone, including digital agreements and breach of confidence, using leading Canadian cases."
    LAW4021H,3,tort-law,"Disputes that arise when one person injures another or damages their property, the competing theories behind tort law, and the alternatives to tort for compensating injury."
    LAW4069H,3,electrification-and-energy-transition-law-and-policy,"The law and regulation of Ontario's energy system and its decarbonisation, from electrifying transport and heating to electricity market structure and renewable deployment."
    LAW4030H,3,financing-technological-innovation,"How technology companies raise money: the financing structures and legal arrangements used in the innovation sector, and the economics that shape them."
    LAW4053H,3,law-and-regulation-banks-and-financial-institutions,The legal and regulatory framework governing banks and financial institutions.
    LAW4063H,3,regulation-artificial-intelligence-legal-and-practical-study,"How artificial intelligence is being regulated around the world: the technical groundwork, the policy frameworks governments have built, and the data privacy law surrounding them."
    LAW4074H,3,immigration-law,"Canada's temporary and permanent immigration pathways and the balance struck between economic policy and human rights obligations, with guest practitioners throughout."
    LAW4028H,3,blockchain-digital-assets-and-law,"How blockchain works and where it is used, then the Canadian legal questions it raises across securities, privacy, tax, anti-money laundering, intellectual property and cybersecurity."
    LAW4022H,3,contract-law,"What makes an agreement binding, what follows when it is broken, the remedies available, and how a contract reaches people who never signed it."
    LAW4031H,3,cybersecurity-and-data-protection-global-information-economy,"The law and policy of cybersecurity: what government and private organisations must do to protect systems and networks, including national security and cross-border questions."
    LAW4075H,3,financial-crime-global-context,"Financial crime across jurisdictions and how corporations and individuals are held to account, from detection through prosecution, including conflicts between national regimes."
    LAW4076H,3,artificial-intelligence-policy-ethics-and-legal-governance,"Where artificial intelligence meets Canadian law and regulation, examined through real applications and set against the approaches taken in the United States, the EU and elsewhere."
    LAW4004H,3,mergers-and-acquisitions,"The law of major corporate transactions, including cross-border deals, worked through real examples of how legal rules meet business practice and negotiation."
    LAW4020H,3,property-law,"Real and personal property in Canadian common law: possession, ownership, adverse possession, estates, easements, and how competing claims to land get resolved."
    LAW4070H,3,ethics-emerging-technology,"The ethical, legal and social questions raised by AI and platforms, with frameworks for responsible development and case studies on bias, privacy and accountability."
    LAW4071H,3,family-law,"Family law past marriage and divorce: parentage, domestic contracts, the rights of unmarried cohabitants and dispute resolution, under both federal and Ontario legislation."
    LAW4023H,3,business-organizations,"Sole proprietorships, partnerships and corporations compared, with the weight on corporate governance and the fiduciary duties directors and officers owe."
    LAW4003H,3,securities-regulation-and-corporate-finance,"How businesses raise capital: exemptions in the private markets, the obligations that come with going public, insider duties, and the regulation of market intermediaries."
    LAW4073H,3,data-law-health-perspective,"Data law applied to health care, across privacy, cybersecurity, intellectual property and AI, for students who will advise or lead inside a health system."
    LAW4024H,3,applied-legal-research-and-writing,"Finding legal information, judging it critically and communicating the answer clearly: the research-to-writing path lawyers take on a hard question."

